<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Volta Redonda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volta-river">Volta</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redonda">Redonda</a> is an industrial city in the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraiba">Paraíba</a> do Sul river. It grew around the steelworks of the National <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">Steel</a> Company, founded in 1941 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/getulio-vargas">Getúlio Vargas</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estado-novo-portugal">Estado Novo</a> with American financing and in production from 1946. The plant was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America</a>'s first large integrated steel mill and a symbol of Brazilian industrialisation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/volta-redonda.jpg" alt="Volta Redonda" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Victor Mauro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pra%C3%A7a_Oscar_Cardoso.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
